            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to set up, then the Kannada for an invitation card."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಬಾಣಂತಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಾಣಂತಿ — bāṇanti — \"a new mother\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಾಣಂತಿ ಮೂರು ತಿಂಗಳು ಅಮ್ಮನ ಮನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಇದ್ದಳು. bāṇanti mūru tiṅgaḷu ammana maneyalli iddaḷu. The new mother stayed three months at her mother's house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman in the weeks after giving birth, looked after with rest, warm food and the home-made ಔಷಧ, medicine, that the elders prepare."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಾಣಂತಿ (bāṇanti) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5347 lists Kannada bāṇanti, \"a woman recently delivered\", beside Malayalam vaṇṇa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
